### Key observations

**Deterministic checks all clean.** 0 contrast pairs, head-term PASS, answer block 51 words, no corpus-count drift, same-type similarity CLEAR (max 0.098 vs threshold 0.04). Body ~3,865 words, under the ceiling. meta_title 56 chars, description 152 — both in band.

**What earns the B+.** The Emmys section is real structural invention, not template — a running-balance scene autopsy that would collapse on any other subject. It produces the signature insight: *"a machine in which other people's self-indulgence visibly takes money from children, and it never once points at him."* The magician's-kid → misdirection thesis passes the swap test harder than anything graded this month, and the two-album-titles find (*Yelled at by a Clown*, *Full Time Magic*) is a genuine discovery. Critic pressure is faced at full strength rather than sanitized, including the AV Club charge that the cleanness *is* the defect. The rabbit hole is the best in the corpus — it argues the losing wing case first, flags its own confidence levels, gives a falsifiability condition, and admits what no type explains.

**The one thing holding it out of A range is provenance, not prose.** The source audit's single "untagged" flag is a false positive (`"Washington's Dream"` is a sketch title), and all three "vague" slots resolve fine in the body. The real problem is that four load-bearing quotes across three clusters rest on mirrors, aggregators, or snippets — most seriously Stephen Bargatze's *"He just didn't show up,"* which carries the TL;DR bullet, FAQ 3, and the whole flunking section, and was read through a scraped Atlantic mirror. RQ-02 is still open by the draft's own admission. Closing that plus the UPtv and THR clusters moves Evidence 8→9 and the overall to **9.2**.

